Because Hong Kong was a territory of the United Kingdom until 1997, Hong Kong law is modeled on UK law, and in the absence of any specific case law to the contrary it is reasonable to assume that the rules will be similar. See {{pg|Commons:Copyright rules by territory/United Kingdom|anchor=TOO|the United Kingdom}} for more details.

